Dear Hiring Team,

I am excited to apply for the Early Career Software Engineer position with Charta Health. I bring more than three years of professional software engineering experience, a Master of Science in Computer Science from Pace University, and a record of turning loosely specified problems into production systems. At Sperse, I delivered an end-to-end Python, TypeScript, and React multi-agent CRM platform that routes requests across 40+ specialized agents for more than 10,000 users—from problem definition through code, tests, and deployment.

That ownership extends into running production systems. I added OpenTelemetry trace-based evaluations and Redis progress tracking to long-running Temporal workflows so the team could locate latency, accuracy, safety, and execution failures. I also built a FastMCP server that gives large language models secure, validated access to 160+ backend actions, then supported smooth deployment with GitHub Actions CI/CD gates. This work required the independence Charta expects: investigating unfamiliar systems, documenting decisions clearly, and driving issues to resolution without waiting for a prescribed path.

Earlier at Qualitest, I delivered a cloud-agnostic Java and Spring Boot storage service spanning Google Cloud Storage, S3, and MinIO, and improved reliability across 100K+ weekly executions with AWS Step Functions. Across both roles, I have learned to care deeply about operational outcomes, debate technical decisions with evidence, and act with intentional urgency—values that align closely with Charta's approach to customer impact.

Charta's mission to make healthcare more affordable and accessible by lowering administrative costs with custom-built AI solutions is especially compelling to me. I would welcome the opportunity to help build the operating system for modern healthcare organizations so providers can focus more capacity on patient care. I can be reached at #ph or #eml. Thank you for your time and consideration; I look forward to connecting.

